    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change updates the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewrote the generation logic:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- `NNNN` = per-city 4-digit sequence, computed as one more than the count of existing owners in that city (`findAll()` filtered by city \u2014 matching the existing pattern; runs before `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created isn't counted yet)\n- Extracted a `prefix3` helper and null-guarded both fields.\n\n**Membership number** (`OwnerMapper.toMembershipNumber`) is formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` and reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` directly, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`) with no code change needed.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` description/example and the `membershipNumber` example to reflect the new format.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass.",
